<article class="env-lemma" id="04T7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04T7">Lemma <span data-tag="04T7">3.9.7</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to S$ be locally of finite type with $X$ quasi-compact. Then $\text{size}(X) \leq \text{size}(S)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We can find a finite affine open covering $X = \bigcup _{i = 1, \ldots n} U_ i$ such that each $U_ i$ maps into an affine open $S_ i$ of $S$. Thus by Lemma <a href="/tag/000Q" data-tag="000Q">3.9.5</a> we reduce to the case where both $S$ and $X$ are affine. In this case by Lemma <a href="/tag/000P" data-tag="000P">3.9.4</a> we see that it suffices to show 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  |A[x_1, \ldots , x_ n]| \leq \max \{ \aleph _0, |A|\} .  \]
</div>
    <p>
       We omit the proof of this inequality. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>